  "notes": "Every grant is bound to a role with the right trust principal, through an inline policy, a managed or IAM policy linked in either direction, or an AWS managed policy. The two Lambda grants of one role cannot be bound to the same role when they sit in separate managed policies, so they are bound to any Lambda role. Name checks also accept a template that creates the named queue, table or topic and references it. The API Gateway grant is not tied to the queue name because the GT uses Resource *. Whether names interpolate Environment is not observable, since parameter refs resolve to their defaults; name checks assume env defaults to dev."
